Use named cases: exercise ordinary content across widths, then concentrate stress cases at the smallest viewport. I’m applying the supplied Flutter responsive-layout skill’s viewport and spatial-contract approach.

The example assumes a **600 logical-pixel breakpoint** and a **320 logical-pixel minimum width**. Replace those with the form’s actual constraints.

| Case | Logical viewport | Content and environment |
|---|---|---|
| Compact | 320 × 720 | Typical |
| Below breakpoint | 599 × 800 | Typical |
| Above breakpoint | 601 × 800 | Typical |
| Wide | 1200 × 900 | Typical |
| Enlarged text | 320 × 720 | Long localized content, 2× text |
| RTL errors | 320 × 720 | Long Arabic content, RTL, validation errors |
| Keyboard | 320 × 720 | Validation errors, focused final field, 300px bottom inset |
| Combined stress | 320 × 720 | Long Arabic content, RTL, errors, 2× text, keyboard |

This keeps failures easy to isolate while adding one deliberate interaction case.

```dart
enum ProfileFixture {
  typical,
  longLocalized,
  longArabicErrors,
  validationErrors,
}

class ProfileCase {
  const ProfileCase(
    this.name,
    this.size, {
    this.fixture = ProfileFixture.typical,
    this.textScale = 1,
    this.locale = const Locale('en'),
    this.direction = TextDirection.ltr,
    this.keyboardInset = 0,
  });

  final String name;
  final Size size;
  final ProfileFixture fixture;
  final double textScale;
  final Locale locale;
  final TextDirection direction;
  final double keyboardInset;
}

const breakpoint = 600.0;

const cases = <ProfileCase>[
  ProfileCase('compact', Size(320, 720)),
  ProfileCase('below breakpoint', Size(breakpoint - 1, 800)),
  ProfileCase('above breakpoint', Size(breakpoint + 1, 800)),
  ProfileCase('wide', Size(1200, 900)),
  ProfileCase(
    'long content with enlarged text',
    Size(320, 720),
    fixture: ProfileFixture.longLocalized,
    locale: Locale('de'),
    textScale: 2,
  ),
  ProfileCase(
    'RTL validation errors',
    Size(320, 720),
    fixture: ProfileFixture.longArabicErrors,
    locale: Locale('ar'),
    direction: TextDirection.rtl,
  ),
  ProfileCase(
    'validation errors with keyboard',
    Size(320, 720),
    fixture: ProfileFixture.validationErrors,
    keyboardInset: 300,
  ),
  ProfileCase(
    'RTL enlarged errors with keyboard',
    Size(320, 720),
    fixture: ProfileFixture.longArabicErrors,
    locale: Locale('ar'),
    direction: TextDirection.rtl,
    textScale: 2,
    keyboardInset: 300,
  ),
];
```

Connect the matrix through one project-specific harness. Have it supply deterministic fixtures through existing dependencies, real localization delegates, a final-field focus node, and an observable submit-attempt callback. Error fixtures should start with validation messages already visible; their submit attempts need not save successfully.

```dart
const visibleBodyKey = ValueKey('profile-visible-body');
const lastFieldKey = ValueKey('profile-last-field');
const saveKey = ValueKey('profile-save');

void expectContained(Rect outer, Rect inner) {
  const tolerance = 0.5;
  expect(inner.left, greaterThanOrEqualTo(outer.left - tolerance));
  expect(inner.top, greaterThanOrEqualTo(outer.top - tolerance));
  expect(inner.right, lessThanOrEqualTo(outer.right + tolerance));
  expect(inner.bottom, lessThanOrEqualTo(outer.bottom + tolerance));
}

void main() {
  for (final scenario in cases) {
    testWidgets('profile: ${scenario.name}', (tester) async {
      final view = tester.view;
      addTearDown(view.reset);
      view.devicePixelRatio = 1;
      view.physicalSize = scenario.size;

      final lastFieldFocus = FocusNode();
      addTearDown(lastFieldFocus.dispose);

      var submitAttempts = 0;

      await tester.pumpWidget(
        MaterialApp(
          locale: scenario.locale,
          // Use the application's actual localization configuration.
          supportedLocales: AppLocalizations.supportedLocales,
          localizationsDelegates:
              AppLocalizations.localizationsDelegates,
          builder: (context, child) => MediaQuery(
            data: MediaQuery.of(context).copyWith(
              textScaler: TextScaler.linear(scenario.textScale),
            ),
            child: Directionality(
              textDirection: scenario.direction,
              child: child!,
            ),
          ),
          home: ProfileTestHarness(
            fixture: scenario.fixture,
            lastFieldFocus: lastFieldFocus,
            onSubmitAttempt: () => submitAttempts++,
          ),
        ),
      );
      await tester.pumpAndSettle();
      expect(tester.takeException(), isNull);

      if (scenario.keyboardInset > 0) {
        lastFieldFocus.requestFocus();
        await tester.pump();

        // DPR is 1, so this is also the logical keyboard height.
        view.viewInsets = FakeViewPadding(
          bottom: scenario.keyboardInset,
        );
        await tester.pumpAndSettle();
        expect(lastFieldFocus.hasFocus, isTrue);
        expect(tester.takeException(), isNull);
      }

      final lastField = find.byKey(lastFieldKey);
      final save = find.byKey(saveKey);
      final visibleBody = find.byKey(visibleBodyKey);

      await tester.ensureVisible(lastField);
      await tester.pumpAndSettle();

      expectContained(
        tester.getRect(visibleBody),
        tester.getRect(lastField),
      );
      expect(
        tester.getRect(lastField).overlaps(tester.getRect(save)),
        isFalse,
        reason: 'Save must not cover the final field.',
      );

      await tester.ensureVisible(save);
      await tester.pumpAndSettle();

      expectContained(
        tester.getRect(visibleBody),
        tester.getRect(save),
      );
      expect(save.hitTestable(), findsOneWidget);

      await tester.tap(save);
      await tester.pumpAndSettle();
      expect(submitAttempts, 1);
      expect(tester.takeException(), isNull);
    });
  }
}
```

Place `profile-visible-body` on the actual safe, keyboard-resized body containing the form and action. Key the final field’s complete region, including its error text. If Save intentionally floats over the scroll area, retain the explicit field/action disjoint assertion after scrolling the field into view.

Add fixture-specific assertions that localized strings and validation messages are present, plus a compact/wide composition assertion at the breakpoint cases. Include one resize test if unsaved values and focus must survive switching compositions. Avoid scanning every render box for intersections.

These are widget-level geometry and interaction checks; the keyboard is simulated. A device test is still needed to verify real OS keyboard behavior. The template above needs your application’s harness and localization imports before it can run.
